<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong><br />
By doing some statistical analysis, the foundation discovers that their information network is being &quot;veiled&quot; from the existance of something. For what appears to be unrelated reasons, a low level reasercher dissapears, leaving behind multiple anomalous object that point to the existance of a society of renaissance cognitohazard wizards.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong><br />
The Foundation's department of analytics, comparing the information flow of various systems, discover that the information flow of the foundation corresponds information flow that has had a &quot;veil&quot; applied to it (Like the veil of normalcy the foundation maintains). A level-4 RAISA officer then breaks into the personal quarters of a junior reasercher, who has vanished, but left behind anomalous objects (the SCP in question). These include various paper drawings of cognitohazardous sigils (<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigil">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigil</a>), and an old book that corresponds mostly to the artes magicae, but includes an 8th type of magic, Infomancy (<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Renaissance_magic">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Renaissance_magic</a>). There are also texts about how to perform &quot;Infomancy&quot;, that is to create infohazardous information by putting together two other non infohazardous peices of information- which then become infohazardous, producing some sort of reaction. Its also revealed that this organisation has been recruiting by creating Infohazards in media that can only be read as recruitment by individuals who meet some prerequisites, like skill, secrecy, desire to join and understanding of their goal.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong><br />
The mystery of what this secret organisation that pulled a reverso uno card on the foundation is, and what their extent and goals are. Also, interesting applications of infohazards and an effective system of hard magic based around them.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong><br />
Ive had this idea for a long time. Using cognitohazards as an effective hard magic system is something ive put a lot of thought into (ive used such a system for a short lived D&amp;D-like thing I did once)</p>

